# This checkout runs with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites line endings on the
# way in and out. For most of the repository that is harmless. For two trees it is
# not, so they are marked -text and pass through byte for byte.
#
# patches/ -- a patch is matched against the pinned IDF, whose files are LF. Give
# the patch CRLF on checkout and every context line stops matching, so `git apply`
# rejects the lot. This is not hypothetical: measuring the delta against the
# upstream fork once reported 7522 changed lines in a file that really had 116,
# for exactly this reason.
#
# bt_overlay/ -- these files are copied verbatim into components/bt and compiled.
# They came from upstream projects and should read the same here as there.

patches/*.patch  -text
bt_overlay/**    -text
